DYECMD
======

This tool is used to dye item graphics used by the Mana client according to the
specification described in docs/dye.md.

Usage:

dyecmd <source_image> <target_image> <dye_string>
dyecmd "<source_image>|<dye_string>" <target_image>
    Recolor source_image using the dye specification and write target_image.

dyecmd analyze <image> [dye]
    Count how many pixels each channel or S/A color pair would affect.

dyecmd instantiate <target> <palettes>
    Print the target with channel placeholders filled from the palette list,
    like SpriteDef does when a sprite path carries a "|" suffix.

e.g.:
dyecmd "armor-legs-shorts.png" "armor-legs-shorts2.png" "W:#222255,6666ff"
dyecmd "armor-legs-shorts.png|W:#222255,6666ff" "armor-legs-shorts2.png"
dyecmd analyze santahat.png "S:#780000,3a3a3a"
